&Q000401 = An adab to Enlil for Šulgi (Šulgi G)
@composite
#project: etcslatf/inter
#atf: use unicode
#atf: use math
#etcsl: text-id=c.2.4.2.07
#key: after http://etcsl.orinst.ox.ac.uk/cgi-bin/etcsl.cgi?text=c.2.4.2.07&display=Crit&charenc=gcirc#

@div sa-gida A

A.1. {d}en-lil₂ gal-di en me-te-na niŋ₂-dug₄-ga-ni zid
#lem: Enlil[1]DN; galdi[exalted]; en[lord]; mete[appropriate thing]; niŋduga[speech]; zid[right]
#tr.en: @wDN{Enlil}, the eminent one, the sovereign lord, whose utterance is trustworthy; @wDN{Nunamnir}, the eternal shepherd of the Land, who hails from the great mountain; the great counsellor, the first and foremost in heaven and on earth, who is in control of all the divine powers; lord, who is imbued with great fearsomeness in accordance with his nobility, a perfected heavenly star, who takes good care of the primeval and choice divine powers, who alone is the lofty god; lord, life-giving light, who leads the people all over the world along one track; huge net spread over heaven and earth, rope stretched over all the lands! Who ever instructed @wDN{Enlil}, who ever rivalled him? 
#etcsl: line-id=A.1

A.2. {d}nu-nam-nir sipad da-ri₂ kalam-ma kur gal-ta e₃-a
#lem: Nunamnir[1]DN; sipad[shepherd]; dari[eternal]; kalam[the Land (of Sumer)]; kur[mountain(s)]; gal[big]; e[leave]
#etcsl: line-id=A.2

A.3. sa₂ gal pad₃-de₃ gu₂-gal an ki me ša-ra u₅-a
#lem: sa[advice]; gal[big]; pad[find]; gugal[foremost]; an[sky]; ki[place]; me[Being]; šar[numerous]V/i; u[ride]
#etcsl: line-id=A.3

A.4. en nam-nun-na-ni-še₃ ni₂ gal im-guru₃ mul-an šu du₇-a
#lem: en[lord]; namnun[magnificence]; ni[fear]; gal[big]; gur[lift]; mulan[heavenly star]; šu[hand]; du[perfect]
#etcsl: line-id=A.4

A.5. me ul me saŋ₅-e gal kiŋ₂-ŋa₂ dili-ni diŋir mah
#lem: me[Being]; ul[distant time]; me[Being]; saŋ[choose]; gal[big]; kiŋ[seek]; dili[single]; diŋir[deity]; mah[great]
#etcsl: line-id=A.5

A.6. en ud til₃ kur-zag til-la-še₃ uŋ₃ dub₃-us₂ dili-a tum₂
#lem: en[lord]; ud[sun]; til[live (of a single person)]; kurzag[mountain border]; til[complete]; uŋ[people]; dus[path]; dili[single]; tum[carry]
#etcsl: line-id=A.6

A.7. sa-par₃ mah an ki šu₂-a eš₂ kur-kur-ra la₂-a
#lem: sabar[net]; mah[great]; an[sky]; ki[place]; šuš[cover]; eš[rope]; kur[mountain(s)]; la[hang]
#etcsl: line-id=A.7

A.8. {d}en-lil₂-da a-ba a₂ mu-da-an-aŋ₂ a-ba-ga-an-da-sa₂
#lem: Enlil[1]DN; aba[who?]; a[arm]; aŋ[measure]; sa[equal]
#etcsl: line-id=A.8

A.9. gal bi₂-dug₄ šag₄-ga-ni id₂ mah a-na-am₃ de₆-a-bi
#lem: gal[big]; dug[speak]; šag[heart]; id[river]; mah[great]; ana[what?]; de[carry]
#tr.en: He thought up something of great importance and he made public what his heart, a mighty river, 
#etcsl: line-id=A.9

A.10. inim kug-ga-na LIL₂ lal₃-ŋar-ra-bi e₂-ta nam-ta-e₃
#lem: inim[word]; kug[pure]; X; lal₃.HI×AŠ₂[subterranean waters]; e[house]; e[leave]
#tr.en: carried: the hidden secrets (?) of his holy thought. 

#etcsl: line-id=A.10

A.11. niŋ₂-bi niŋ₂ kug-ga-am₃ niŋ₂ šen-nam me e₂-kur-ra-kam
#lem: niŋ[thing]; niŋ[thing]; kug[pure]; niŋ[thing]; šen[pure]; me[Being]; Ekur[1]TN
#tr.en: The matter is a holy and pure one, it concerns the divine powers of the @wTN{E-kur}, 
#etcsl: line-id=A.11

A.12. šeg₁₂ zid nam tar-ra abzu sa-dur₂-ra niŋ₂ kal-kal-la-am₃
#lem: šeg[brick]; zid[right]; nam[fate]; tar[cut]; abzu[(cosmic) underground water]; sadur[bottom]; niŋ[thing]; kal[rare]
#tr.en: the fated good brick embedded (?) in the bottom of the @fsux{abzu}, it is something most important: 
#etcsl: line-id=A.12

A.13. e₂-kur lu₂ zid-de₃ i₃-du₃-e mu da-ri₂-kam
#lem: Ekur[1]TN; lu[person]; zid[right]; du[build]; mu[name]; dari[eternal]
#tr.en: a trustworthy man will rebuild the @wTN{E-kur}, thereby acquiring a lasting name. 
#etcsl: line-id=A.13

A.14. dumu lu₂ zid-da-ke₄ ŋidru mi-<ni>-ib₂-su₃-ra₂ {ŋiš}gu-za-bi nu-kur₂
#lem: dumu[child]; lu[person]; zid[right]; ŋidru[scepter]; sud[distant]; guza[chair]; kur[different]
#tr.en: The son of this trustworthy man will long hold the sceptre, and their throne will never be overthrown. 
#etcsl: line-id=A.14

A.15. nam-bi-še₃ e₂-kur-ra sig₇ mi-ni-ŋar {d}aš!-im₂-babbar-re
#lem: nam[fate]; Ekur[1]TN; sissig[green-yellow]; ŋar[put]; Dilimbabbar[1]DN
#tr.en: To that end, @wDN{Ašimbabbar} appeared shining in the @wTN{E-kur}, pleaded to his father @wDN{Enlil} and made him bring a childbearing mother (?); 
#etcsl: line-id=A.15

A.16. a-a-ni {d}en-lil₂ inim-ma bi₂-sig₁₀ ama di-da mi-ni-in-de₆
#lem: aya[father]; Enlil[1]DN; inim[word]; sig[put into]; ama[mother]; utud[give birth (to)]; de[carry]
#tr.en: in the @wTN{E-duga}, @wDN{Nanna}, the princely son, asked for the thing to happen. 
#etcsl: line-id=A.16

A.17. e₂-dug₃-ga {d}nanna dumu nun-ne₂ niŋ₂ al ba-ni-dug₄
#lem: Eduga[1]TN; Nanna[1]DN; dumu[child]; nun[prince]; niŋ[thing]; al[cvne]; dug[speak]
#tr.en: The @fsux{en} priestess gave birth to the trustworthy man from his semen placed in the womb. 
#etcsl: line-id=A.17

A.18. en-ne₂ <a> šag₄-tur-še₃ ŋal₂-la-na lu₂ zid mi-ni-u₃-tud
#lem: en[priest]; a[water]; šagtur[womb]; ŋal[⟦be⟧ to be (there]; lu[person]; zid[right]; utud[give birth (to)]
#tr.en: @wDN{Enlil}, the powerful shepherd, caused a young man to emerge: a royal child, 
#etcsl: line-id=A.18

A.19. {d}en-lil₂ sipad a₂ kalag-ga-ke₄ meš₃-e pa bi₂-e₃
#lem: Enlil[1]DN; sipad[shepherd]; a[arm]; kalag[strong]; mes[hero]; pa[branch]; e[leave]
#tr.en: one who is perfectly fitted for the throne-dais, 
#etcsl: line-id=A.19

A.20. dumu nam-lugal barag-ge₄ he₂-du₇ šul-gi lugal-am₃
#lem: dumu[child]; namlugal[kingship]; barag[sanctum]; hedu[ornament]; Šulgir[1]RN; lugal[king]
#tr.en: @wRN{Šulgi} the king. 
#etcsl: line-id=A.20

A.21. a piriŋ-ŋa₂ <e₂>-kur šu daŋal-la dug₄-dug₄ ki aŋ₂ {[d]}[nin]-lil₂-la₂
#lem: a[water]; piriŋ[lion]; Ekur[1]TN; šu[hand]; daŋal[wide]; dug[speak]; ki[place]; aŋ[measure]; Ninlil[1]DN
#tr.en: @wDN{Enlil} gave him a good name: 'A lion's seed, who provides the @wTN{E-kur} generously, 
#etcsl: line-id=A.21

A.22. e₂-kur-ta nam-nir-ŋal₂ šum₂-ma lugal urim₅#{[ki]}-ma
#lem: Ekur[1]TN; namnirŋal[authority]; šum[give]; lugal[king]; Urim[1]SN
#tr.en: the beloved one of @wDN{Ninlil}; the one granted authority in the @wTN{E-kur}; the king of @wSN{Urim}, 
#etcsl: line-id=A.22

A.23. šag₄ zalag-zalag sipad {d}lamma kalam-ma mu-ni bi₂#-in#-dug₃
#lem: šag[heart]; zalag[bright]; sipad[shepherd]; lammar[(female) tutelary deity]; kalam[the Land (of Sumer)]; mu[name]; dug[good]
#tr.en: the one with shining heart, the shepherd, the protective genius of the Land'. 
#etcsl: line-id=A.23

A.24. šul-gi {d}en-lil₂-le šag₄ kug-ge bi₂-pad₃ kalam šu-ni bi₂-si
#lem: Šulgir[1]RN; Enlil[1]DN; šag[heart]; kug[pure]; pad[find]; kalam[the Land (of Sumer)]; šu[hand]; si[fill]
#tr.en: @wDN{Enlil} chose @wRN{Šulgi} in his pure heart and entrusted the Land to him. 
#etcsl: line-id=A.24

A.25. šibir ešgiri₂ a₂-na mu-ni-la₂ sipad kur-kur-ra-kam
#lem: šibir[shepherd's staff]; ešgiri[staff]; a[arm]; la[hang]; sipad[shepherd]; kur[mountain(s)]
#tr.en: As the shepherd of all the countries, @wDN{Enlil} leant the crook and the staff against his arm, 
#etcsl: line-id=A.25

A.26. ŋidru {d}nanna šu nu-bal-e šu-ni-še₃ mu-ŋar
#lem: ŋidru[scepter]; Nanna[1]DN; šu[hand]; bala[turn]; šu[hand]; ŋar[put]
#tr.en: and placed the immutable sceptre of @wDN{Nanna} in his hand; he made him raise his head high, 
#etcsl: line-id=A.26

A.27. dur₂ nam-lugal sag₂ nu-di-da gu₂ an-še₃ mi-ni-zig₃
#lem: dur[buttocks]; namlugal[kingship]; sag[scatter]; di[speak]; gu[neck]; an[sky]; zig[rise]
#tr.en: sitting on an unshakeable royal seat. 
#etcsl: line-id=A.27

A.28. ud šudu₃-dam ŋi₆ nam-šita-am₃ kalam u₂-sal-la-am₃
#lem: ud[sun]; šud[prayer]; ŋi[night]; namšita[prayer]; kalam[the Land (of Sumer)]; usal[meadow]
#tr.en: The day was for prayers, the night was for supplications; the Land rested in peace. 
#etcsl: line-id=A.28

A.29. sipad he₂-ŋal₂-la šul-gi mu gi₁₆-sa lugal asilₓ(EZEN)-le₂
#lem: sipad[shepherd]; heŋal[plenty]; Šulgir[1]RN; mu[name]; gilsa[treasure]; lugal[king]; asilala[joy]
#tr.en: The shepherd of prosperity, @wRN{Šulgi}, he with a lasting name, the king of jubilation, 
#etcsl: line-id=A.29

A.30. kalag-ga a lu₂ zid-de₃ ri-a {d}en-lil₂ mu-i-i
#lem: kalag[strong]; a[water]; lu[person]; zid[right]; ri[impose]; Enlil[1]DN; e[bring out]
#tr.en: the mighty one, the semen engendered by the faithful man, praised @wDN{Enlil}. 
#etcsl: line-id=A.30

@div trailer 

A.31. sa-gid₂-da-am₃
#lem: sagida[musical notation]
#tr.en: This is the @fsux{sa-gida}. 
#etcsl: line-id=A.31

@end trailer

@end sa-gida

@div ŋišgiŋal B

B.32. šul#-[gi] lugal uru₁₆ [...] ku-kur silim-e-eš₂ dug₄-ga
#lem: Šulgir[1]RN; lugal[king]; urun[exalted]; X; kurku[wish]; silim[healthy]; dug[speak]
#tr.en: @wRN{Šulgi}, the mighty king, ……, who exults in his triumph, 
#etcsl: line-id=B.32

B.33. lugal# X aga₃-kar₂ {d}inana ki-bal-a bi₂-sig₁₀
#lem: lugal[king]; X; agakar[conquest]; Inanak[1]DN; kibala[rebel land]; sig[put into]
#tr.en: the …… king vanquished the rebellious land with the @fsux{agakar} weapon of @wDN{Inana}. 
#etcsl: line-id=B.33

@div trailer 

B.34. ŋiš-gi₅-ŋal₂ sa-gid₂-da-kam
#lem: ŋešgiŋal[musical refrain]; sagida[musical notation]
#tr.en: It is the @fsux{ŋišgiŋal} of the @fsux{sa-gida}. 
#etcsl: line-id=B.34

@end trailer

@end ŋišgiŋal

@div sa-ŋara C

C.35. {d}en-lil₂ zid-da-am₃ inim-ma-ni mah-am₃
#lem: Enlil[1]DN; zid[right]; inim[word]; mah[great]
#tr.en: May @wDN{Enlil} the trustworthy, 
#etcsl: line-id=C.35

C.36. nam dug₃ tar-ra-ni saŋ-bi-še₃ e₃-a-am₃
#lem: nam[fate]; dug[good]; tar[cut]; saŋ[head]; e[leave]
#tr.en: whose words are lofty -- good fate determined by him takes precedence -- who makes sturdy flax and barley grow -- may he prolong the life of @wRN{Šulgi}, 
#etcsl: line-id=C.36

C.37. gu niŋ₂ kalag mu₂-mu₂ še niŋ₂ kalag mu₂-mu₂
#lem: gu[cord]; niŋ[thing]; kalag[strong]; mu[grow]; še[barley]; niŋ[thing]; kalag[strong]; mu[grow]
#tr.en: the provider of the @wTN{E-kur} -- hence its flax is indeed fine flax, 
#etcsl: line-id=C.37

C.38. šul-gi e₂-kur-ra u₂-a-bi na-nam
#lem: Šulgir[1]RN; Ekur[1]TN; ua[provisioner]; me[be]
#tr.en: its barley is indeed fine barley -- the property of @wDN{Nanna}, 
#etcsl: line-id=C.38

C.39. gu-bi gu na-nam še-bi še na-nam
#lem: gu[cord]; gu[cord]; me[be]; še[barley]; še[barley]; me[be]
#tr.en: the houseborn-slave of the @wTN{E-kur}, 
#etcsl: line-id=C.39

C.40. niŋ₂-u₂-rum {d}nanna ama-tud e₂-kur-ra
#lem: niŋurum[property]; Nanna[1]DN; amaʾatud[house-born slave]; Ekur[1]TN
#tr.en: him whom @wDN{Ninlil} named at his birth @wRN{Šulgi}, 
#etcsl: line-id=C.40

C.41. šag₄-ta mu pad₃#-da {d}nin-lil₂-la₂ na-nam
#lem: šag[heart]; mu[name]; pad[find]; Ninlil[1]DN; me[be]
#tr.en: the shepherd of the Land, 
#etcsl: line-id=C.41

C.42. šul-gi sipad kalam-ma saŋ {d}en-lil₂-le zu
#lem: Šulgir[1]RN; sipad[shepherd]; kalam[the Land (of Sumer)]; saŋ[head]; Enlil[1]DN; zu[know]
#tr.en: the man whom @wDN{Enlil} knows, 
#etcsl: line-id=C.42

C.43. e₂-a lu₂-bi na-nam ud he₂-em-ma-ab-su₃-re₆
#lem: e[house]; lu[person]; me[be]; ud[sun]; sud[distant]
#tr.en: the steward of the temple. 
#etcsl: line-id=C.43

C.44. urim₅{ki} iri{ki} dug₃ nun-ne₂ ki ŋar-ra
#lem: Urim[1]SN; iri[city]; dug[good]; nun[prince]; ki[place]; ŋar[put]
#tr.en: So that its voluminous offering meals would bring joy to the @wTN{E-kur}, 
#etcsl: line-id=C.44

C.45. šag₄-bi dub-šen kug abzu igi nu-bar
#lem: šag[heart]; dubšen[treasure chest]; kug[purify]; abzu[(cosmic) underground water]; igi[eye]; bar[place outside]
#tr.en: @wDN{Enlil} called upon @wSN{Urim}, the good city founded by the princely one, 
#etcsl: line-id=C.45

C.46. nam#-išib dug₃-ga-kam šu-luh dadag-ga-kam
#lem: namišib[office of išib-priest]; dug[good]; šuluh[ritual cleansing]; dadag[bright]
#tr.en: the inside of which is a holy treasure chest which, like the @fsux{abzu}, 
#etcsl: line-id=C.46

C.47. nidba gal-gal-bi e₂-kur hul₂-le-de₃
#lem: nindaba[(food) offering]; gal[big]; Ekur[1]TN; hul[rejoice]
#tr.en: no eye can see -- the city of good purification rites and pure hand-washing rites; 
#etcsl: line-id=C.47

C.48. {d}en#-lil₂-le gu₃ ba-an-de₂ dug₄#-ga!(BI) zid-zid-dam
#lem: Enlil[1]DN; gu[voice]; de[pour]; dug[speak]; zid[right]
#tr.en: and what he says is trustworthy. 
#etcsl: line-id=C.48

C.49. sipad nam-lugal-la barag mah-ha tum₂-ma
#lem: sipad[shepherd]; namlugal[kingship]; barag[sanctum]; mah[great]; tum[suitable]
#tr.en: For his setting up the abundant sacrificial tin cups, 
#etcsl: line-id=C.49

C.50. šul-gi nam-en-na tug₂-ba₁₃ sud-sud-am₃
#lem: Šulgir[1]RN; namen[the office of en-priest]; ba[garment]; sud[distant]
#tr.en: for his having served evening meals in the dining-hall of the @wTN{E-kur}, 
#etcsl: line-id=C.50

C.51. bur!# an-naₓ(AN) he-nun-na sug₂-sug₂-ga-ni-še₃
#lem: bur[(stone) bowl]; anna[metal]; henun[plenty]; sug[stand]
#tr.en: @wDN{Enlil} determined a princely fate for the shepherd, 
#etcsl: line-id=C.51

C.52. unu₂ e₂-kur#-ra-ka kiŋ₂-sig gub#-ba#-ni-še₃#
#lem: unu[dwelling]; Ekur[1]TN; kiŋsig[afternoon meal]; gub[stand]
#tr.en: him who is worthy of the kingship and the lofty throne-dais, 
#etcsl: line-id=C.52

C.53. {d}en-lil₂ nam-nun-na [mu]-ni#-in-tar-e#
#lem: Enlil[1]DN; namnun[magnificence]; tar[cut]
#tr.en: @wRN{Šulgi}, who is adorned with the @fsux{ba} garment of the @fsux{en} priests. 
#etcsl: line-id=C.53

C.54. an-gin₇ sig₇-ga-ni X [...]-e#
#lem: an[sky]; sissig[green-yellow]; X; X
#tr.en: The one beautiful like heaven, ……, 
#etcsl: line-id=C.54

C.55. {d}nanna lugal-am₃ [...]-am₃#
#lem: Nanna[1]DN; lugal[king]; X
#tr.en: @wDN{Nanna}, the king, 
#etcsl: line-id=C.55

C.56. ki-ur₃ ki gal-la# [...] dug₃# mu-na#-šum₂
#lem: Kiʾur[1]; ki[place]; gal[big]; X; dug[good]; šum[give]
#tr.en: the ……, gave him good …… in the @wTN{Ki-ur}, 
#etcsl: line-id=C.56

C.57. {d}en-lil₂-la₂ KA# [...] mu#-ši-daŋal-e
#lem: Enlil[1]DN; X; X; daŋal[wide]
#tr.en: the great place. At the command (?) of @wDN{Enlil}, 
#etcsl: line-id=C.57

C.58. kur a nun gi₄-a gu₂-un-gu₂-un# mu-na-ab-za
#lem: kur[mountain(s)]; a[arm]; nun[prince]; gi[turn]; gungugu[an animal noise]; za[cvve]
#tr.en: he ……, he roars for him (?) against the foreign land that no one dare oppose. 
#etcsl: line-id=C.58

C.59. ma-da mu-gen₆-ge-en₆# uŋ₃ ŋiri₃-ni-še₃ mu-nu₂
#lem: mada[land]; gin[confirm]; uŋ[people]; ŋiri[foot]; nud[lie down]
#tr.en: He stabilizes the countryside, and the people lie at his feet. 
#etcsl: line-id=C.59

C.60. šul-gi sipad lu₂-lal₃! nibru{ki} ki aŋ₂-am₃
#lem: Šulgir[1]RN; sipad[shepherd]; lulal[dear]; Nibru[1]SN; ki[place]; aŋ[measure]
#tr.en: @wRN{Šulgi}, the shepherd is the honey man beloved by @wSN{Nibru}; may the true shepherd, @wDN{Šulgi}, refresh himself in the pleasant shade of @wDN{Enlil's} brickwork! 
#etcsl: line-id=C.60

C.61. šeg₁₂ {d}en-lil₂-la₂ ŋissu-bi dug₃-ga-am₃
#lem: šeg[brick]; Enlil[1]DN; ŋissu[shade]; dug[good]
#etcsl: line-id=C.61

C.62. sipad zid šul-gi-re ni₂ he₂-em-ši-ib₂-ten-ten
#lem: sipad[shepherd]; zid[right]; Šulgir[1]RN; ni[self]; ten[extinguish]
#etcsl: line-id=C.62

@div trailer 

C.63. sa-ŋar-ra-am₃
#lem: saŋara[musical notation]
#tr.en: It is the @fsux{sa-ŋara}. 
#etcsl: line-id=C.63

@end trailer

@end sa-ŋara

@div ŋišgiŋal D

D.64. šul-gi bal-za {d}en-lil₂-le ud dug₃ ma-ra-ni-in-e₃
#lem: Šulgir[1]RN; bala[turn]; Enlil[1]DN; ud[sun]; dug[good]; e[leave]
#tr.en: O @wRN{Šulgi}, @wDN{Enlil} has brought forth happy days for you in your reign! 
#etcsl: line-id=D.64

@div trailer 

D.65. ŋiš-gi₅-ŋal₂ sa-ŋar-ra-kam
#lem: ŋešgiŋal[musical refrain]; saŋara[musical notation]
#tr.en: It is the @fsux{ŋišgiŋal} of the @fsux{sa-ŋara}. 
#etcsl: line-id=D.65

@end trailer

@end ŋišgiŋal

@div uru E

E.66. an-na lugal-be₂-e ki-a kur gal-be₂-e
#lem: an[sky]; lugal[king]; ki[place]; kur[mountain(s)]; gal[big]
#tr.en: Heaven's king, earth's great mountain, Father @wDN{Enlil}, heaven's king, earth's great mountain, thought up something great: he chose @wDN{Šulgi} in his heart for a good reign! 
#etcsl: line-id=E.66

E.67. a-a {d}en-lil₂ an-na lugal-be₂-e ki-a kur gal-be₂-e
#lem: aya[father]; Enlil[1]DN; an[sky]; lugal[king]; ki[place]; kur[mountain(s)]; gal[big]
#etcsl: line-id=E.67

E.68. gal bi₂-dug₄ šul-gi bal zid-da šag₄-ge-eš i-pad₃
#lem: gal[big]; dug[speak]; Šulgir[1]RN; bala[turn]; zid[right]; šag[heart]; pad[find]
#etcsl: line-id=E.68

@div trailer 

E.69. u₁₈-ru₁₂-NI-bi-im
#lem: uru[literary subscript]
#tr.en: It is its @fsux{uru}. 
#etcsl: line-id=E.69

@end trailer

@end uru

@div trailer 

